§ `Chapters 23 to 32 -- exactions and the Crown's officers`

§§ `Chapter 23 -- bridges`

-- gloss (not the text's): "from of old legally bound" is taken as a plain fact.
-- src:53 | No community or individual shall be compelled to make bridges at river banks, except those who from of old were legally bound to do so.
@ref Chapter 23 (src:53)
GIVEN `from of old they were legally bound to make bridges at river banks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 23 -- a community or individual may be compelled to make a bridge at a river bank` IS
    IF `from of old they were legally bound to make bridges at river banks`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except those who from of old were legally bound to do so".
    THEN `Not barred`
    ELSE Barred

§§ `Chapter 24 -- pleas of the Crown`

-- "No sheriff, constable, coroners, or others of our bailiffs": a bailiff stands for "others of our
-- bailiffs".  The King and the chief justiciar are not named and the answer for them is `Bar not covered`.
-- src:55 | No sheriff, constable, coroners, or others of our bailiffs, shall hold pleas of our Crown.
@ref Chapter 24 (src:55)
GIVEN officer IS A Party
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 24 -- the officer may hold pleas of the Crown` IS
    IF   officer EQUALS `a sheriff`
      OR officer EQUALS `a constable`
      OR officer EQUALS `a coroner`
      OR officer EQUALS `a bailiff`
    THEN Barred
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

-- src:55 | No sheriff, constable, coroners, or others of our bailiffs, shall hold pleas of our Crown.
@ref Chapter 24 (src:55)
GIVEN officer IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 24 -- no sheriff, constable, coroner or other bailiff shall hold pleas of the Crown` IS
    IF `ch 24 -- the officer may hold pleas of the Crown` officer EQUALS Barred
    THEN PARTY officer
         SHANT `hold pleas of the Crown`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY officer BECAUSE "ch 24: an officer held pleas of the Crown"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `Chapter 25 -- the old rents`

