      `the rent demanded` IS A NUMBER
      `an additional payment is demanded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 25 -- the rent or payment demanded of this unit may be demanded` IS
    CONSIDER unit
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(except our demesne manors)" -- the exception takes the demesne manors out of the rule.
    WHEN `a demesne manor` THEN `Not barred`
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: except because "except" removes the demesne manors, which has its own branch; this branch is reached by a unit the text does not name).
    WHEN `some other unit` THEN `Bar not covered`
    OTHERWISE IF   `the rent demanded` GREATER THAN `the old rent`
                OR `an additional payment is demanded`
              THEN Barred
              -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: except because "except" removes the demesne manors, which has its own branch; for the other units "shall remain at the old rents" carries no named word (F25, F64c)).
              ELSE `Bar not covered`

