      `he tenders money for it immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller permits postponement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 28 -- the officer may take corn or other provisions in this way` IS
    IF   officer EQUALS `a constable`
      OR officer EQUALS `a bailiff`
    THEN IF `the seller permits postponement`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he can have postponement thereof by permission of the seller".
         THEN `Not barred`
         ELSE IF `he tenders money for it immediately`
              -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: unless because "unless" governs only the postponement; the tender limb is "without immediately tendering money", which is not a named word (F64c)).
              THEN `Bar not covered`
              ELSE Barred
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: unless because "unless" qualifies when a constable or bailiff may take; the branch is reached by an officer other than those named).
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

-- src:63 | No constable or other bailiff of ours shall take corn or other provisions from any one without immediately tendering money therefor, unless he can have postponement thereof by permission of the seller.
