§§ `Chapter 32 -- the lands of persons convicted of felony`

-- "one year and one day": the last day is the day a year on from the starting day, plus one day.
-- The text does not say from what day it is counted (fork F32), so the starting day is an input.
-- A starting day of 29 February has no day a year on; the standard library's `add years` gives
-- 28 February (fork F32b).
-- src:71 | We will not retain beyond one year and one day, the lands of those who have been convicted of felony, and the lands shall thereafter be handed over to the lords of the fiefs.
@ref Chapter 32 clause 32.1 (src:71)
GIVEN start IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `ch 32 -- the last day the King may retain the lands` IS
    `add years` start 1 PLUS 1

-- src:71 | We will not retain beyond one year and one day, the lands of those who have been convicted of felony, and the lands shall thereafter be handed over to the lords of the fiefs.
@ref Chapter 32 clause 32.1 (src:71)
GIVEN `the lands are those of a person convicted of felony` IS A BOOLEAN
      start IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 32 -- the King may retain the lands on this day` IS
    IF `the lands are those of a person convicted of felony`
    THEN IF day AT MOST `ch 32 -- the last day the King may retain the lands` start
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "we will not retain beyond one year and one day" (a limit the text states).
         THEN `Not barred`
         ELSE Barred
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

-- src:71 | We will not retain beyond one year and one day, the lands of those who have been convicted of felony, and the lands shall thereafter be handed over to the lords of the fiefs.
@ref Chapter 32 clause 32.1 (src:71)
GIVEN `the lands are those of a person convicted of felony` IS A BOOLEAN
      start IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 32 -- the King will not retain the lands beyond one year and one day` IS
    IF `ch 32 -- the King may retain the lands on this day` `the lands are those of a person convicted of felony` start day EQUALS Barred
    THEN PARTY `the King`
         SHANT `retain the lands of a convicted felon beyond one year and one day`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 32: the lands of a person convicted of felony were retained beyond one year and one day"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- "the lands shall thereafter be handed over to the lords of the fiefs" (passive, fork F32c).
-- src:71 | We will not retain beyond one year and one day, the lands of those who have been convicted of felony, and the lands shall thereafter be handed over to the lords of the fiefs.
@ref Chapter 32 clause 32.1 (src:71)
GIVEN `the lands are those of a person convicted of felony` IS A BOOLEAN
      start IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `ch 32 -- the lands are handed over to the lords of the fiefs` IS
    IF `the lands are those of a person convicted of felony`
    THEN IF day GREATER THAN `ch 32 -- the last day the King may retain the lands` start
         THEN Obliged
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "thereafter" dates the handing over; it does not say that none is owed before then (F64c).
         ELSE `Obligation not covered`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Obligation not covered`
